374: #  ANSWERS to a CEILING frozen at landing: for each row, phase, seat, date, d and note, no more answers than the md5-pinned
375: #  baseline holds.  Not a date (a date-only cutoff cannot stop a back-dated or undated addition), not a count without the
376: #  note (a converted entry's allowance could be refilled; pass 2), and NOT an entry identity: a byte-identical revert of a
377: #  normalised entry passes, and the dashboard's legacy count can still rise through exempt records and re-exposed older
378: #  answers (adjudication pass, GPT-6 Astra).  HARD.  It fails on UNMATCHED content and on an EXCESS occurrence -- a NEW
379: #  off-domain answer, or an OLD one edited in any of those fields (an admitted replacement can be new; v3 pass): editing such an entry means classifying it -- a glyph, no `d`, or a non-answer record token (Fable
380: #  5.1); for a note-only correction that toll is this check's, not the ruling's (Grok 4.7).  It reds (rc 2) when the ledger
381: #  or the baseline is unreadable or misshapen or the baseline's md5 is not the pinned one, never silently green.
382: say ""; say "Q2. a ledger answer carries a d the dashboard classifies, or is within the frozen legacy ceiling"
